@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ============================================================================
### 0. HEALTH CHECK (Actuator)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 1. API v2 - CRIAR EVENTO (CONCERT -> Taxa de 15% via SOLID Strategy)
### No IntelliJ IDEA, o bloco > {% ... %} salva o ID automaticamente em {{eventId}}!
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Rock in Rio - Noite do Metal",
  "description": "Show principal no Palco Mundo",
  "category": "CONCERT",
  "eventDate": "2027-09-15T20:00:00",
  "totalCapacity": 500,
  "basePrice": 200.00
}

> {%
    client.global.set("eventId", response.body.id);
%}

### ============================================================================
### 2. API v2 - CRIAR EVENTO (WORKSHOP -> Taxa de 5% via SOLID Strategy)
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Workshop Spring Boot 4 e Java 25",
  "description": "Imersao pratica em arquitetura backend",
  "category": "WORKSHOP",
  "eventDate": "2027-10-20T09:00:00",
  "totalCapacity": 40,
  "basePrice": 100.00
}

### ============================================================================
### 3. API v2 - LISTAR TODOS OS EVENTOS
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 4. API v2 - FILTRAR EVENTOS POR CATEGORIA (CONCERT, WORKSHOP, CONFERENCE)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events?category=WORKSHOP
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 5. API v2 - CONSULTAR POR ID (Retorna objeto 'pricing' detalhado)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events/{{eventId}}
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 6. VERSIONAMENTO DE API - URI v1 LEGADA (Retorna 'price' + Header Deprecation)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 7. VERSIONAMENTO DE API - VIA HEADER (X-API-Version: 1 vs 2)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}
X-API-Version: 1
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}
X-API-Version: 2
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 8. API v2 - ATUALIZAR EVENTO (PUT)
### ============================================================================

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events/{{eventId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Rock in Rio - Noite do Metal (Lote Extra)",
  "description": "Show principal no Palco Mundo - Capacidade ampliada",
  "category": "CONFERENCE",
  "eventDate": "2027-09-15T20:00:00",
  "totalCapacity": 800,
  "basePrice": 250.00
}

### ============================================================================
### 9. TESTES DE ERRO (RFC 7807 ProblemDetail)
### ============================================================================

### 9a. Erro de validacao (422 Unprocessable Content)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "WORKSHOP",
  "eventDate": "2027-10-10T10:00:00",
  "totalCapacity": 0,
  "basePrice": -10.00
}

### 9b. Recurso nao encontrado (404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 10. API v2 - DELETAR EVENTO (204 No Content)
### ============================================================================

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events/{{eventId}}


### ============================================================================
### 11. FASE 2 - MIGRATIONS COM FLYWAY (Inspecionar tabela flyway_schema_history)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/flyway
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 12. FASE 2 - ÍNDICES NO BANCO (Executar EXPLAIN e ver o Index Scan em ação)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/query-plan?category=CONCERT
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 13. FASE 2 - TRANSAÇÕES ACID: COMPRAR INGRESSOS (Com Lock Otimista @Version)
### Salva automaticamente o ID do pedido em {{orderId}} no IntelliJ IDEA!
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{eventId}}",
  "customerEmail": "caike@flashticket.com",
  "quantity": 2,
  "usePessimisticLock": false,
  "simulateFailureAfterStockDeduction": false
}

> {%
    client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id);
%}

### ============================================================================
### 14. FASE 2 - TRANSAÇÕES ACID: TESTAR ROLLBACK ATÔMICO
### Simula erro logo APÓS abater o estoque no banco. O @Transactional fará
### ROLLBACK automático e o availableTickets do evento NÃO será reduzido!
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{eventId}}",
  "customerEmail": "caike@flashticket.com",
  "quantity": 10,
  "usePessimisticLock": false,
  "simulateFailureAfterStockDeduction": true
}

### ============================================================================
### 15. FASE 2 - CONSULTAR PEDIDOS DO CLIENTE (Usa índice idx_ticket_orders_customer_email)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/orders?customerEmail=caike@flashticket.com
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================================
### 16. FASE 3 - ZERAR O CONTADOR DE QUERIES SQL (Antes de testar o N+1)
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/sql-counter/reset

### ============================================================================
### 17. FASE 3 - GRAPHQL COM PROBLEMA DE QUERIES N+1 (@SchemaMapping individual)
### Dispara 1 SELECT para eventos + N SELECTs para cada pedido (N+1 queries!)
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { eventsWithNPlusOneProblem { id title category availableTickets finalPrice orders { id customerEmail quantity totalAmount status } } }"
}

### ============================================================================
### 18. FASE 3 - VER QUANTOS SELECTs FORAM EXECUTADOS NO BANCO (Veja o N+1!)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/sql-counter
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 19. FASE 3 - ZERAR O CONTADOR E TESTAR A SOLUÇÃO COM @BatchMapping (DataLoader)
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/sql-counter/reset

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { eventsOptimized { id title description category availableTickets basePrice platformFee finalPrice orders { id customerEmail quantity totalAmount status } } }"
}

### ============================================================================
### 20. FASE 3 - COMPROVAR QUE O @BatchMapping EXECUTOU APENAS 2 SELECTs!
### (1 SELECT em events + 1 SELECT ... WHERE event_id IN (...) em ticket_orders)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/sql-counter
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================================
### 21. FASE 4 - TESTAR CACHE-ASIDE (@Cacheable: CACHE MISS vs CACHE HIT)
### Passo 1: Zere o contador SQL, depois chame o GET 2 vezes seguidas e olhe o
### sql-counter: na 1ª chamada faz 1 SELECT (Miss), na 2ª faz 0 SELECTs (Hit)!
### ============================================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/sql-counter/reset

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/events/{{eventId}}
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/diagnostics/sql-counter
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 22. FASE 4 - CONSULTAR DOCUMENTOS NOSQL DE AUDITORIA (MongoDB Audit Logs)
### Repare como o campo 'flexiblePayload' muda de estrutura conforme a ação
### (EVENT_CREATED vs TICKET_PURCHASED vs EVENT_UPDATED) sem usar Migrations!
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/audit-logs
Accept: application/json

### Filtrar documentos NoSQL de auditoria por ID do evento
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/audit-logs?resourceId={{eventId}}
Accept: application/json



### ============================================================================
### FASE 5: SEGURANÇA DE PONTA A PONTA (JWT, ROTAÇÃO DE REFRESH TOKEN, OAUTH 2.0,
###         CORS, CSRF, XSS & RATE LIMITER COM TOKEN BUCKET)
### ============================================================================

### 23. Login Stateless -> Emite Access Token (JWT HS256) + Refresh Token (#1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "caike@flashticket.com",
  "password": "Flash@2026"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken1", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 24. Acessar rota protegida (/api/v2/auth/me) enviando o JWT no Header Authorization: Bearer
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 25. Rotação de Refresh Token (Uso Único): Troca Refresh Token #1 por um novo par (#2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken1}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken2", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 26. SIMULAÇÃO DE ROUBO DE TOKEN (Reuse Detection):
### Tente enviar o Refresh Token #1 antigo uma 2ª vez -> O servidor detecta reuso
### e REVOGA TODA A FAMÍLIA DE TOKENS (inclusive o Refresh Token #2)!
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken1}}"
}

### 27. OAuth 2.0 — Fluxo 1: Authorization Code Flow com PKCE (S256)
### Passo 27A: Gerar par PKCE (code_verifier secreto + code_challenge S256)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/oauth2/pkce-helper
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.global.set("pkceVerifier", response.body.codeVerifier);
    client.global.set("pkceChallenge", response.body.codeChallenge);
%}

### Passo 27B: Solicitar Authorization Code enviando apenas o code_challenge (S256)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/oauth2/authorize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientId": "flashticket-web-spa",
  "userEmail": "caike@flashticket.com",
  "redirectUri": "https://app.flashticket.com/callback",
  "codeChallenge": "{{pkceChallenge}}",
  "codeChallengeMethod": "S256",
  "state": "estado_anti_csrf_123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("oauthCode", response.body.authorizationCode);
%}

### Passo 27C: Trocar o Authorization Code por Tokens enviando o code_verifier original
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grantType": "authorization_code",
  "clientId": "flashticket-web-spa",
  "code": "{{oauthCode}}",
  "codeVerifier": "{{pkceVerifier}}"
}

### 28. OAuth 2.0 — Fluxo 2: Client Credentials Flow (Máquina-a-Máquina / M2M para Parceiros)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grantType": "client_credentials",
  "clientId": "flashticket-partner-gateway",
  "clientSecret": "partner-secret-2026",
  "scope": "tickets:read webhooks:write"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("partnerToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### Acessar endpoint exclusivo de parceiro M2M (ROLE_PARTNER)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/security-demo/partner-only
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 29. Demonstração de XSS Sanitization, CSRF Double-Submit Cookie e Rate Limiter (429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/security-demo/sanitize-xss
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rawHtml": "<script>alert('XSS')</script><img src=x onerror=\"roubarToken()\">Show Rock in Rio"
}

### Rate Limiter (Token Bucket): Rode 6 vezes seguidas para ver o 429 Too Many Requests na 6ª chamada!
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/security-demo/rate-limited
X-Client-Key: meu-ip-teste
Accept: application/json



### ============================================================================
### FASE 6: PROGRAMAÇÃO ASSÍNCRONA (@Async), WEBHOOKS (HMAC + IDEMPOTÊNCIA)
###         E CRON JOBS / TAREFAS AGENDADAS (@Scheduled)
### ============================================================================

### 30. Gerar assinatura HMAC-SHA256 para testar o Webhook Inbound de Pagamento
### (Antes de rodar o 30, certifique-se de ter rodado o passo 1 e o passo 13 para ter um {{orderId}}!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/webhooks/payment/sign-helper
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "webhookEventId": "evt_gateway_001",
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "paymentStatus": "PAID"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("webhookSignature", response.body.signatureHeaderValue);
%}

### 31. Enviar Webhook Inbound (Valida X-Webhook-Signature, garante Idempotência e dispara @Async)
### (Rode 2 vezes seguidas para ver duplicateIgnoredByIdempotency = true na 2ª vez!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/webhooks/payment
X-Webhook-Signature: {{webhookSignature}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "webhookEventId": "evt_gateway_001",
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "paymentStatus": "PAID"
}

### 32. Consultar o comprovante de QR Code gerado em background pela thread @Async (FlashTicket-Async-*)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/async/fulfillments/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json

### 33. Listar Webhooks Outbound enviados pelo FlashTicket para o sistema do Organizador
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/webhooks/outbound-deliveries
Accept: application/json

### 34. Cron Job (@Scheduled): Forçar expiração de um pedido PENDING e rodar limpeza para devolver estoque
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/jobs/expire-order-for-test/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/jobs/run-expired-orders-cleanup
Accept: application/json



### ============================================================================
### FASE 7: PADRÕES DE RESILIÊNCIA EM INTEGRAÇÕES EXTERNAS
###         (TIMEOUTS, RETRIES + EXPONENTIAL BACKOFF/JITTER, CIRCUIT BREAKER,
###          BULKHEAD E FALLBACK)
### ============================================================================

### 35. Retry com Exponential Backoff + Jitter:
### Simula falha 503 nas tentativas #1 e #2 e sucesso na tentativa #3!
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v2/resilience/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 250.00,
  "behavior": "TRANSIENT_FAIL_TWICE_THEN_SUCCEED"
}

### 36. Erro permanente de negócio (422 Cartão Recusado):
### Comprova que erros 4xx NÃO sofrem Retry (attemptsMade = 1) e NÃO abrem o Circuit Breaker!
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v2/resilience/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 250.00,
  "behavior": "NON_RETRYABLE_CARD_DECLINED_422"
}

### 37. Timeout + Fallback:
### Simula Gateway travado demorando mais que o limite -> Aborta nas 3 tentativas e enfileira no Fallback (202 Accepted)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v2/resilience/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 250.00,
  "behavior": "SLOW_TIMEOUT"
}

### 38. Circuit Breaker (Rode 3 vezes para atingir o failureThreshold e abrir o disjuntor -> OPEN)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v2/resilience/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 250.00,
  "behavior": "ALWAYS_FAIL_503"
}

### 39. Inspecionar status do Circuit Breaker (OPEN), vagas do Bulkhead e fila de Fallback
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v2/resilience/status
Accept: application/json

### 40. Transicionar Circuit Breaker para HALF_OPEN e enviar 1 chamada saudável para fechar o circuito (CLOSED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v2/resilience/circuit-breaker/transition-half-open
Accept: application/json

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v2/resilience/charge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 250.00,
  "behavior": "HEALTHY_SUCCESS"
}
